in whole milliseconds since 1970"}]}]]],"header":"row"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The session is the only identifier sent: there is no "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"user_id"},{"type":"text","text":", and no "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ip"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"idfv"},{"type":"text","text":" or other"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"device identifier. Amplitude counts a user per "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"device_id"},{"type":"text","text":", so its unique users are sessions. A"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"record with no session (one tracked by a tracker without "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Enricher.sessions()"},{"type":"text","text":") is its own"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"anonymous user, linked to nothing: Amplitude rejects an event with neither a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"device_id"},{"type":"text","text":" nor a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"user_id"},{"type":"text","text":". Amplitude drops a second copy of an event with the same "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"insert_id"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"device_id"},{"type":"text","text":"."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"A record a store recovers after a relaunch keeps its session, so it goes out with the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"device_id"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"session_id"},{"type":"text","text":" of its first send, and Amplitude drops it if it had already stored"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"it before the app ended. The"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"record’s vendor identifier and trace context, and any other context value, aren’t sent. Nor is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"an "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ip"},{"type":"text","text":": neither an address nor "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"$remote"},{"type":"text","text":", which asks Amplitude to look the user’s location up"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"from the request’s address."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Properties are read through the event’s schema in "},{"code":"plan","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", as "},{"code":"PropertyReader","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" reads them. A"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events\/Sensitive","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" value is never sent, whatever the record reveals: the property is left"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"out, an element of an array is "},{"code":"null","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", and one inside a type the plan can’t map is "},{"code":"null","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Amplitude limits each string value to 1,024 characters; the encoder sends longer ones as they"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"are."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Each event also holds these members, for each of the keys the record’s context has a value","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"for:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"table","rows":[[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Member"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Key","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Holds"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"app_version","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ApplicationKey"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The version, left out when "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"nil"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"device_model","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DeviceKey"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The model","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"language"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"LocaleKey","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The locale’s BCP 47 identifier, such as ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"en-US"},{"text":", which Amplitude stores as the language’s name","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"platform"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"os_name"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"os_version"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"OperatingSystemKey","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The operating system’s name, its name again, and its version"}],"type":"paragraph"}]]],"header":"row"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A record the encoder can’t write is left out of the request, and the batch’s other records are","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"sent: one whose event and version ","type":"text"},{"code":"plan","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" doesn’t describe, one whose event name Amplitude keeps","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"for its own events, one whose event isn’t ","type":"text"},{"code":"Encodable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", one that holds a value JSON can’t, one","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"whose timestamp has no epoch-milliseconds form, and one too large for a request","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/AmplitudeEncoding\/documentation\/AmplitudeEncoding\/AmplitudeEncodingError","type":"reference"},{"text":"). ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/AmplitudeEncoding\/documentation\/AmplitudeEncoding\/AmplitudeBatchEncoder\/requests(for:)","type":"reference"},{"text":" returns them as ","type":"text"},{"code":"SkippedRecord","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"s, which","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"HTTPDestination","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" logs and reports on its ","type":"text"},{"code":"dropReports","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/AmplitudeEncoding\/documentation\/AmplitudeEncoding\/AmplitudeBatchEncoder\/requests(for:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" splits a batch into requests within the encoder’s limit, "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/AmplitudeEncoding\/documentation\/AmplitudeEncoding\/AmplitudeBatchEncoder\/batchLimit","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" by"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"default, and makes none for a batch with no record it can write, so "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDestination"},{"type":"text","text":" sends"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"nothing for it. Amplitude answers a request it takes with 200, so "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDestination"},{"type":"text","text":" retries"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"one that gets no response, a 5xx, 408 or 429, and drops one it rejects, such as with 400 or"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"413. A record sent again keeps its "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"insert_id"},{"type":"text","text":". The bytes are the same for the same records on"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"every run and platform: no whitespace, object members in the order of their names’ UTF-8"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"bytes."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/amplitudeencoding\/amplitudebatchencoder"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"sections":[],"kind":"symbol","hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/AmplitudeEnco